      <processInformation>
        <referenceFunction amount="1.0" category="electronics" datasetRelatesToProduct="true" generalComment="The dataset can be used as a seperator membrane between a cathode and an anode, e.g. for a lithium-ion battery. Data are based on patents. For infrastructure, the ecoinvent dataset &quot;chemical plant, organics&quot; is accounted. Transportation efforts are based on ecoinvent standard estimates.;&#10;UUID: 1e15c5f4-d81a-35a2-b262-e495f647b22d" includedProcesses="This dataset incudes the production of a seperator for a lithium-ion battery. Polyethylene foil is coated with a slurry composed of silica, a Co-polymere of  PVDF (proxy: PVF) and hexafluor ethane and dibutyl phthalate (proxy: phthalic anhydride). The polytehylene foil is coated on 1 side with the slurry. Then, the coated foil is dried in a &quot;dry channel&quot; (H2O content &lt; 20 ppm) and coiled up. The same procedure is done for the second side of the collector foil." infrastructureProcess="false" localCategory="electronics" localName="Separator, lithium-ion battery, at plant" localSubCategory="devices\module\component" name="Separator, lithium-ion battery, at plant" subCategory="devices\module\component" unit="kg"/>
        <geography location="CN" text="&lt;null&gt;"/>
        <technology text="This dataset includes a method of producing a seperator for a lithium ion battery. The seperator seperates anode from cathode, but allows an exchange of Li+-ions through micropores. In case of to high process temperature of the battery, the seperator melts,  thus  closes the micopores, interrupts the Li+-ion exchange and therefore stops the chemical process and pretends finally from  overheating or a burning battery . "/>
